# localswarm profile — machine-specific settings. Copy to:
#   ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/localswarm/profile.env
# (or point LOCALSWARM_PROFILE at another file). Every value is optional; defaults are shown.
# Run scripts/swarm_check.sh to probe your endpoint and print suggested values.
# Do NOT put secrets in this file — tokens go in the .env file below.

# ---- Model endpoint ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the model API INCLUDING its path prefix. Agents' requests are forwarded to
# <base>/messages + <base>/models (Anthropic format) or <base>/chat/completions + <base>/models
# (OpenAI format). Examples:
#   http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1         local vLLM / SGLang
#   https://llm.example.com/v1       remote gateway
#   https://webui.example.com/api    Open WebUI (OpenAI format)
#SWARM_LLM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1

# API format of the endpoint: anthropic | openai | auto (probe once when the bridge starts).
# Claude Code only speaks Anthropic Messages; for "openai" the bridge translates requests and
# responses, including streaming and tool calls.
#SWARM_API_FORMAT=auto

# Model id. Empty = first model the endpoint lists. Pin it when the endpoint lists several.
#SWARM_MODEL=

# Upstream read timeout in seconds (long generations need a long one).
#SWARM_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT=3600

# ---- Authentication ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bearer token for the endpoint, read ONLY by the host bridge (and by claude-local in direct
# mode). It never enters an agent sandbox and is never logged.
# The file holds lines like:  SWARM_API_TOKEN=xxxxxxxx   (quotes and "export " are allowed).
# Keep it private: chmod 600. A variable of the same name in the environment takes precedence.
#SWARM_ENV_FILE=${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/localswarm/.env
#SWARM_TOKEN_VAR=SWARM_API_TOKEN

# ---- Effort and thinking -------------------------------------------------------------------
# How swarm effort levels map to the effort string your endpoint accepts.
# Swarm levels: off | low | medium | high. ("off" disables thinking and sends the "low" value.)
# Some servers reject "high" and use "xhigh" instead — swarm_check.sh tells you.
#SWARM_EFFORT_MAP="low=low medium=medium high=high"

# JSON merged into the request's chat_template_kwargs when effort is "off".
# Qwen-style templates use enable_thinking; other model families may differ.
#SWARM_THINK_OFF_KWARGS='{"enable_thinking": false}'

# ---- Sandbox network and paths -------------------------------------------------------------
# Extra host suffixes the sandbox may never reach (space separated), e.g. your own domains.
# Loopback, private, link-local and reserved IPs are always refused. (The bridge itself may
# still talk to the model endpoint on such a domain; this only limits the agents.)
#SWARM_BLOCK_SUFFIXES=""

# Where the bridge puts its unix sockets, log and pid file. Default: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/localswarm-<uid>
#SWARM_SOCK_DIR=

# Host TCP port for the bridge's model route, used by claude-local (needed for --effort off,
# OpenAI-format endpoints, and prefixes other than /v1). Empty = no TCP listener.
#SWARM_BRIDGE_TCP_PORT=

# Extra read-only paths to mount into every sandbox (colon separated), e.g. an SDK outside /usr.
# Toolchains (node, npm, npx, git, python3, claude) found outside /usr are mounted automatically;
# extra CLIs to treat the same way: SWARM_EXTRA_TOOLS="java gradle"
#SWARM_EXTRA_RO=
#SWARM_EXTRA_TOOLS=

# Port the in-sandbox HTTPS proxy listens on (private to each sandbox; rarely needs changing).
#SWARM_PROXY_PORT=3128

# Commit identity used by agents.
#SWARM_GIT_NAME="Local Swarm Agent"
#SWARM_GIT_EMAIL=swarm-agent@localhost
